  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1400</x>
      <y>40</y>
      <w>400</w>
      <h>190</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Conventions
--
Storage: idx = i + W·(j + H·k), x fastest
Sizes: powers of two; height = 0 → 1D,
depth = 0 → 2D
Forward is unnormalised, inverse = forward × 1÷N
True ND DHT = separable passes + Bracewell
correction; ForwardSeparable skips it
(valid for convolution with even kernels)
GPU: compute in float (FP64 is 1:64 on GeForce)
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1400</x>
      <y>270</y>
      <w>400</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>«external»
--
OpenMP — required
CUDA runtime + cuBLAS — RAPIDHT_WITH_CUDA=ON
MPI — RAPIDHT_WITH_MPI=ON, experimental:
  more than one process throws (B-002)
bg=#FFFFFF</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1400</x>
      <y>440</y>
      <w>400</w>
      <h>140</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>«consumers, link coreht»
--
tests — GoogleTest; checked against the
  O(N²) definition and analytic pairs
benchmarks — Google Benchmark; cuFFT and
  FFTW baselines; profile_gpu3d for Nsight
examples — fdht1d, fdht2d, fdht3d
bg=#FFFFFF</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1400</x>
      <y>620</y>
      <w>400</w>
      <h>140</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Build
--
Library target: coreht (static unless BUILD_SHARED_LIBS)
backend_cuda.cpp and kernels.cu are compiled in
only with RAPIDHT_WITH_CUDA=ON. Without them the
GPU members are stubs, and the constructor
rejects Modes::GPU at runtime
bg=#FFFFE0</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
